                <pb facs="0893" n="797" sameAs="frus:frus1921v02/pg797"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">361.1121 K 55/130: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Commissioner at Riga</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Young</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Riga</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-06-24T13:00:00+01:36"><hi rendition="#italic">June 24, 1921—1
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received June 25—5:06
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>446. Department’s 71, June 23rd, 5 p.m. My telegram 444, June 21st, repeated to
                    London and Christiania. I do not believe that such pressure as Baltic Provinces
                    might be able to exert would be effective <pb facs="0894" n="798" xml:id="pg798"
                    /> unless it included possible stoppage transit trade and this these states
                    would hardly be prepared to do especially in view our attitude in matter of
                    their recognition.</p>
                <p>I believe they would be very willing to make official representations on our
                    behalf but such representations would not in all probability be effective.</p>
                <p>I suggest for Department’s consideration that release of our citizens be
                    immediately demanded through Bolshevik mission at Reval or Riga and that failing
                    prompt compliance with this demand an embargo be at once placed on all shipments
                    for Soviet Russia and the entry of American citizens into Soviet Russia
                    prohibited.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Young</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
